Package: ash
Version: @DEB_VERSION@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-pip, ca-certificates
Maintainer: awslabs <awslabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/awslabs/automated-security-helper
Description: Automated Security Helper (ASH) security scan orchestrator
 ASH runs a suite of security scanners over a source tree and aggregates their
 findings into a single report, in SARIF and several other formats.
 .
 This package installs ASH itself. It does not bundle any scanner: the scanners
 ASH drives are third-party tools, and shipping their source inside this package
 is forbidden by the project's artifact-contents rule. Install them with
 "ash dependencies install", optionally selecting individual tools with --tool.
 .
 The post-install step needs a reachable Python package index to resolve ASH's
 runtime dependencies. On a host with no index, stage one first; see
 /usr/share/doc/ash/README.Debian for why the package cannot carry them.
